Shared hosting (OVHcloud) sets opcache.restrict_api to its own status script,
so opcache_invalidate() raises "Zend OPcache API is restricted" on every call.
Drupal 11.4 calls it for each PHP file the hook collector reads; the installer
prints every warning, sends headers early and fails to start its session.
Invalidation cannot happen on such hosts anyway: silence the warning only.

--- a/core/lib/Drupal/Component/Utility/OpCodeCache.php
+++ b/core/lib/Drupal/Component/Utility/OpCodeCache.php
@@ -33,7 +33,9 @@
 
     // Check if the Zend OPcache is enabled and if so invalidate the file.
     if (function_exists('opcache_invalidate')) {
-      opcache_invalidate($pathname, TRUE);
+      // Hosts that set opcache.restrict_api answer with a warning: there is
+      // nothing to invalidate from here, so the warning is suppressed.
+      @opcache_invalidate($pathname, TRUE);
     }
   }
 
